<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">
    <h1 style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # <span style="font-style: italic;">[Insert Theme Number Here]</span> – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #333; padding: 10px; text-align: center; margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a5276;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">SECTION 2 — LESSON IDENTIFICATION TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Time Capsule</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Preparing for the Next Five Years</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Show comprehension of everyday conversations, with some repetition of particular words and phrases. Interactive: Respond appropriately when participating in discussions on familiar topics.</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can identify and summarize key points from a conversation about career plans, including relevant advice (e.g., "The speaker plans to pursue software development and will take an internship with a local Panamanian tech company."). Can respond appropriately when participating in discussions on familiar topics and summarize peers' plans (e.g., "Carlos said that he is interested in studying marine biology."). Can comprehend and summarize ideas in a conversation about career advice (e.g., "The podcast suggested that you should reach out to local organizations to meet mentors in areas you are interested in for work.").</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">SECTION 3 — AOA STAGES TABLE</h2>
    <table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
                <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f0f0f0; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing a short, engaging video clip (30-45 seconds) featuring young people talking about their dreams for the future. After the video, the teacher displays images of various career paths (e.g., software developer, engineer, doctor, community service leader). Students are asked to briefly mention one thing they hope to <b>achieve</b> in the next five years, activating prior knowledge about future aspirations. The teacher writes down key vocabulary heard from students on the board.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary words related to future plans and careers: <i>career, goals, possibilities, advice, internship, skills, leadership, problem-solving, achieve, pursue, develop, future-oriented</i>. The teacher models the pronunciation of these words, explicitly focusing on the long vowel /iː/ in words like "achieve," "believe," "volunteer," and "engineering" (even if not all are introduced, the sound is modeled). Stress in multisyllabic words like "leadership," "problem-solving," and "critical thinking" is also highlighted. For example, "I might <b>pursue</b> a <b>career</b> in <b>technology</b>."</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher uses visuals and examples to ensure understanding of the new vocabulary.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you want to work as a software developer, is that a hobby or a <b>career</b>?" (Expected answer: "A career.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If you spend time learning about new computer programs, are you <b>developing skills</b> or just playing games?" (Expected answer: "Developing skills.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule")</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students will listen to an audio recording (3-4 minutes) of two Panamanian high school students, Sofia and Daniel, discussing their post-graduation <b>future plans</b> and career <b>goals</b> for the next five years. They talk about subjects they enjoy, potential university studies, and ideas for internships or volunteer work. One student mentions wanting to become a <b>software developer</b> and possibly doing an <b>internship</b>, while the other is interested in <b>engineering</b> and developing <b>problem-solving skills</b>. The conversation includes some advice they've received.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will demonstrate receptive listening comprehension of everyday conversations on familiar topics related to future plans and career advice.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First Listening (Gist):</b> Students listen for the main idea. "What is the main topic of Sofia and Daniel's conversation?" (A) Their favorite TV shows. (B) Their future plans after high school. (C) Their recent vacation.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second Listening (True/False & Matching):</b> Students listen again for specific details.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Task 1: True or False statements (e.g., "Sofia wants to become a doctor." "Daniel is considering a career in engineering.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Task 2: Match the speaker to their plan (e.g., "Sofia" to "plans to pursue software development," "Daniel" to "wants to develop problem-solving skills").</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice identifying and extracting specific grammatical structures (modals for possibilities, future continuous for ongoing plans, reported speech for advice) and target vocabulary from the audio. They will focus on active listening for these specific elements.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice (Cloze/Gap-fill):</b> The teacher provides a transcript of short excerpts from the audio with gaps for key target vocabulary (e.g., <i>internship, skills, pursue, advice</i>) and grammar structures (e.g., "I <b>might pursue</b>...", "I <b>will be working as</b>...", "My teacher <b>said that I should</b>..."). Students listen to the audio a third time, pausing after each excerpt to fill in the missing words or phrases. This activity reinforces vocabulary and grammatical forms.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher plays specific sentences or short segments from the audio again. Students are given sentence stems on a worksheet and complete them based on what they hear, focusing on future plans and advice. For example: "Sofia said that she ___________ (verb) in an IT company to gain <b>experience</b>." or "Daniel thinks he ____________ (modal) study <b>engineering</b> because he likes <b>problem-solving</b>." This helps them practice listening for modals and future continuous.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Check & Reported Speech:</b> In pairs, students compare their answers from the previous activities. They then practice reporting what they heard. For instance, one student might say, "Sofia <b>said that she might pursue</b> software development," and the other responds, "Yes, and she also <b>mentioned that she will be gaining</b> <b>experience</b> in an internship." This activity encourages them to use reported speech based on the listening input, as well as the target vocabulary.</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule")</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative group discussion and sharing (in groups of 3-4).</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students work in small groups to discuss their own "future plans" for a hypothetical "time capsule" project, inspired by Sofia and Daniel's conversation. Each student takes turns sharing one or two specific goals they hope to <b>achieve</b> in the next five years, using modals (e.g., "I <b>might consider</b> studying <b>medicine</b>," "I <b>will be developing</b> my <b>leadership skills</b> through volunteer work") and future continuous. One student in each group acts as a "recorder" (sociolinguistic competence), taking notes on their peers' plans. After each group member shares, the others can ask clarifying questions or offer "advice" based on what they heard, using reported speech (e.g., "Carlos, you <b>said that you are interested</b> in marine biology; my uncle <b>suggested that you should research</b> local environmental organizations"). This activity focuses on active listening to peers and responding appropriately.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to Theme and Scenario:</b> Students directly engage with "How I Am Preparing for the Next Five Years" by articulating their own plans, and the "time capsule" scenario provides a context for future reflection. The activity promotes active listening as students gather and summarize information about their peers' goals.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in discussing future goals, collaborative interaction, and accurate comprehension of peers' plans for later summarization.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation using a simple checklist to note students' listening comprehension and ability to summarize information from the audio and their peers. The teacher will specifically look for use of target vocabulary, modals, and reported speech, as well as clear pronunciation of /iː/ sounds and stressed words.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group "presenter" (sociolinguistic competence) briefly summarizes one or two key <b>goals</b> from their group members to the class, based on their recorder's notes. For example, "Carlos <b>said that he is interested</b> in studying marine biology, and Ana <b>will be working</b> on her <b>critical thinking skills</b> for a <b>career</b> in <b>data analysis</b>." Other students listen actively.</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Comprehension:</b> Accurately identifies and summarizes key points from peers' plans (Listening outcome).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Use of Target Language:</b> Appropriately uses target vocabulary (e.g., <i>career, goals, internship, skills</i>), modals for possibilities (<i>might, could</i>), and reported speech (<i>said that he/she will be, suggested that I should</i>).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Clarity & Pronunciation:</b> Delivers summaries with intelligible pronunciation, including clear long /iː/ sounds and appropriate stress in multisyllabic words.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. <b>Collaboration:</b> Participates effectively in group discussion and note-taking.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "Today, I feel I successfully listened to and understood ___________ (e.g., career advice, my friends' future plans)."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "One new word or phrase about future plans that I learned today is ___________."</li>
                    </ul>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompts:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What specific strategies did I use today to help me understand the conversations I listened to?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "How will listening to conversations about future plans help me plan my own path?"</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What aspects of the listening activities worked well, and what challenges did students face?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did students effectively use the new vocabulary and grammar (modals, future continuous, reported speech)? Were the pronunciation points clear?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or additional scaffolds (e.g., providing a word bank for listening, more repetition) might be needed for Lesson 2 to ensure comprehension of the same core vocabulary in a reading context?"</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson introduced key vocabulary and grammar related to future plans through listening. In Lesson 2 (Reading Comprehension), students will encounter a written text on a similar topic, using the same core vocabulary (e.g., <i>career, goals, internship, skills, advice, pursue, develop</i>) to deepen their contextual understanding and reading skills.</p>
                </td>
                <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                    <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Time]</p>
                </td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>